---
import PageLayout from "@/layouts/Base.astro";

const meta = {
	description: "About the Western Massachusetts Clean Energy Network.",
	title: "About",
};
---

<PageLayout meta={meta}>
	<h1 class="title mb-12">About the Western Massachusetts Clean Energy Network</h1>
	<div class="prose prose-sm prose-cactus max-w-none">
		<p>
			We are a small, informal group of Western Massachusetts residents working on clean energy, siting, and forest stewardship. Members include academics, consultants, business owners, nonprofit volunteers, and retired community members with decades of local knowledge. We meet in person and on email.
		</p>
		<p>
			The Massachusetts energy transition is happening unevenly across the state. Cities have rooftops. Rural towns have land. The state law that took effect in 2024 sets new rules about who decides what. We exist to help residents and town officials understand those rules and the choices they create.
		</p>
		<h2>What we do</h2>
		<p>
			We follow how state and local rules shape what gets built where. Massachusetts changed those rules in 2024 with Chapter 239. We read the regulations and translate them for residents and town officials.
		</p>
		<p>
			Public debate over solar siting is full of claims about land use, forest carbon, panel safety, and ratepayer cost. We check those claims against evidence and publish what we find.
		</p>
		<p>
			We meet, we draft, we share. Members come from academic research, the solar industry, town committees, retired professional life, and civic groups across Hampshire and Franklin counties.
		</p>
		<p>
			We do not represent any agency, university, or company. Members are speaking for themselves.
		</p>
	</div>
</PageLayout>
